acpi: retire Notify

The interpreter puts Notify (Object, Value) in flight but has no case
for it when its operands are done, so it panicked with "Unexpected
operation has created in-flight op!": a ThinkPad T15's _INIs notify.
The handler has no notification hook and nothing in myos listens for
them, so the op only retires.

Derived from acpi, so under acpi's license (MIT or Apache-2.0).

--- a/src/aml/mod.rs
+++ b/src/aml/mod.rs
@@ -983,6 +983,14 @@
                             context.retire_op(op);
                         }
                     }
+                    Opcode::Notify => {
+                        /*
+                         * The firmware tells the OS about an event on a device (a battery's
+                         * status changed, a dock, a thermal trip). The handler is not asked:
+                         * nothing here listens for notifications, so the op only retires.
+                         */
+                        context.retire_op(op);
+                    }
                     _ => panic!("Unexpected operation has created in-flight op!"),
                 }
             }
